// A scenery object with a track reference: the glTF plus the pose its author
// meant. The route editor's object tool drops it at exactly this lateral
// offset, rotation and height; every placed instance stores concrete values
// and can deviate (lines/*.ron, `objects:`).
//
// lateral_offset: metres, positive = right of increasing arc length.
// yaw_deg: rotation about up, clockwise from above; 0 = front along the track.
// height: metres above the railhead.
(
    name: "Mast",
    model: "example/assets/sig_mast.gltf",
    lateral_offset: -3.5,
    yaw_deg: 0.0,
    height: 0.0,
)
